    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access permitted. Please use the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a viewing.\r\n\r\nCharming four-bedroom home is set on approximately 1.4 acres of beautiful grounds, offering picturesque views of the surrounding countryside. Built around two decades ago, the home is filled with natural light, creating a bright and welcoming atmosphere. The location is highly convenient, with three towns accessible within a 20-minute drive. Drinagh Village, providing essential amenities such as a supermarket, hardware store, churches, school, and several pubs, is only a 20-minute walk from the property. 1 hours drive to Cork City & Aiport\r\nThe Loung/diner is thoughtfully designed to maximise natural brightness, featuring numerous windows that flood the space with light. Two sets of French doors open directly onto the garden, seamlessly connecting the indoor living area with the outdoors and allowing for uninterrupted views of the grounds. A wood-burning stove serves as the centrepiece of the room, providing warmth and a cosy atmosphere throughout the year.\r\nThe kitchen is exceptionally well designed, occupying a central position within the home and serving as the heart of daily living. It is fully fitted and finished to a high standard, with an emphasis on maximising natural light to create a bright and airy atmosphere. A convenient door leads directly from the kitchen to a separate utility room, providing additional space for laundry and storage needs, and enhancing the overall practicality of the living area. \r\nThe ground floor includes a spacious master bedroom, which is again bright, light, and airy. The master benefits from an ensuite bathroom and a walk-in dressing room for added convenience. Additionally, there is another generously sized bedroom and a ground floor WC.\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nAccessed by a spacious stone driveway, the private garden covers around 1.6 acres and offers breathtaking elevated views of the countryside.  Mainly laid to lawn  with a sitting area which is perfect for relaxing and making the most of the glorious view. The garden, which can be accessed easily, is enclosed by mature trees, light woodland, shrubs, and wildflowers, creating a habitat that supports local wildlife.\r\nThe property includes a spacious outbuilding serving as a garage and workshop, with upstairs accommodation featuring a bedroom, kitchen, utility room, living area, and wet room. Behind the house is  an unfinished building suitable for conversion to stables, kennels, or storage.   A wooden studio sits between the house and garage/workshop.\r\n\r\nThis property  has joint agency with \r\nHodnett Forde Property Services, \r\nNegotiator: Liam Hodnett MIPAV\r\nPhone: 087 246 4152 or  023 883 3367 \r\nEmail: liam@hodnettforde.com or info@hodnettforde.com\r\n\r\nGeneral Disclaimer / Important Notice\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
      },
